verdicts.evidence:
Verified against DRBD 9.3.2 at HEAD a46cbd9440cb (both /tmp/drbdsrc and /home/tommy/projects/drbdsrc_clone confirmed at same commit; cited lines byte-identical in both).

(1) LOCATION CONFIRMED. drbd_main.c:4947 `static bool __new_current_uuid_prepare(struct drbd_device *device, bool forced)`; function spans 4947-4977.

(2) BODY CONTENTS CONFIRMED, exact lines:
  4953  spin_lock_irq(&device->ldev->md.uuid_lock);
  4954  day0 = drbd_uuid_is_day0(device);
  4955  got_new_bitmap_uuid = rotate_current_into_bitmap(...);
  4965  val = get_random_u64();
  4966  __drbd_uuid_set_current(device, val);
  4967  spin_unlock_irq(&device->ldev->md.uuid_lock);
  4970  err = drbd_md_sync(device);
All three named calls present, in order.

(3) NO SUSPEND/QUORUM GATE IN BODY — CONFIRMED. The five callees in the body (drbd_uuid_is_day0, rotate_current_into_bitmap @4837, get_random_u64, __drbd_uuid_set_current @4747-4757, drbd_md_sync) were read; none contain drbd_suspended/have_quorum/may_inc_ap_bio. __drbd_uuid_set_current (4747) only does drbd_md_mark_dirty + role-flag set + write current_uuid + drbd_uuid_set_exposed. grep for those three tokens in drbd_main.c finds them ONLY in unrelated functions (have_quorum @2710/4275-4276, drbd_suspended @3456), never inside 4947-4977.

ADVERSARIAL CHECK — the guards exist, but in the CALLERS, not the body, which is exactly what the (narrowly-scoped) claim says:
  - drbd_sender.c:3443  `if (device->have_quorum[NOW] && drbd_data_accessible(device, NOW)) drbd_uuid_new_current(...)` — quorum gate on the MAKE_NEW_CUR_UUID worker dispatch.
  - drbd_req.c:2262 comment `/* check need for new current uuid _AFTER_ ensuring IO is not suspended via may_inc_ap_bio */`, gated by may_inc_ap_bio @2257 — app-write path gate.
  - drbd_state.c:4466 `if (!susp_uuid[OLD] && susp_uuid[NEW] && test_and_clear_bit(NEW_CUR_UUID,...)) new_current_uuid = true; ... drbd_uuid_new_current(device, false)` — fires on the suspend->thaw (susp_uuid) transition. (This is the line the project memory cites; it is a susp_uuid-transition gate, not an unguarded call. The bump here happens when IO is being RESUMED out of suspension, not while frozen.)
None of these gates are inside __new_current_uuid_prepare, so the claim's narrow assertion 'the function body has NO such check' is literally true.

(4) LOG LINE: line number 4981 CONFIRMED, but the quoted string is TRUNCATED. cat -A of 4981-4982 shows the actual format string is `"new current UUID: %016llX weak: %016llX\n"` (function __new_current_uuid_info @4979). The claim's quote `'new current UUID: %016llX'` is a correct prefix but omits the ` weak: %016llX` suffix. This is the only inaccuracy and is cosmetic; it does not affect the substantive finding.

OFFICIAL DOCS corroborate the design intent: DRBD 9 on-no-quorum defaults to suspend-io (drbdsetup-9.0 / drbd.conf-9.0 manpages; LINBIT user guide) — a quorum-lost primary freezes IO rather than erroring, and the UUID-bump is meant to be dispatched only when IO is allowed (the drbd_req.c:2262 _AFTER_ comment and the drbd_sender.c:3443 have_quorum gate enforce this upstream of the leaf function). Verdict: CONFIRMED with one minor quoting nit on the log string.
